{"type":"message","id":"4e6cefb2","parentId":"094e14db","timestamp":"2026-05-29T00:30:29.204Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only heartbeat messages - no human discussion. The last heartbeat in both threads was at 23:45 UTC. Current time is 00:30 UTC, so I need to send the 00:30 UTC heartbeat.\n\nLet me calculate the current status:\n- Started at 15:05 UTC\n- Current time: 00:30 UTC next day = 29.5 hours later = 1770 minutes\n- Wait, let me recalculate: 15:05 to 00:30 next day is 9 hours 25 minutes = 565 minutes? No wait...\n- Actually 15:05 to midnight is 8h55m = 535 minutes, then to 00:30 is another 30 minutes = 565 minutes total from 15:05 to 00:30 next day\n\n\n- But I need to account for crossing into the next calendar day - from 15:05 on the 28th to 00:30 on the 29th is indeed 9 hours 25 minutes or 565 minutes\n- Though that seems like a large gap from the 746-minute readings at 23:45, I should verify whether my time conversion is off or if there's actually been a significant pause between heartbeats\n\n.\n\nNow I'm seeing timestamps from both arbitration and general threads that correspond to around 23:50 UTC, but the current time shows 00:30 UTC - a 40-minute gap. I need to calculate how many minutes have passed since the session started at 15:05 UTC on May 28th.\n\nFrom 15:05 to midnight is 8 hours 55 minutes, then from midnight to 00:30 on May 29th adds another 30 minutes, totaling 9 hours 25 minutes or 565 minutes. The percentage would be 565 divided by 2660 total minutes, which gives about 21.2% - but that feels off compared to the previous reading of 28.0% at 746 minutes. Let me reconsider whether 15:05 might actually be in a different timezone or if I'm missing something about how the minutes are being calculated. I see the timestamps are actually Unix epoch values in milliseconds—I can verify this by converting msg_1778975171553 to 2026-05-28 23:46:11 UTC, which aligns with the heartbeat time